---
import ContentPage from "../components/ContentPage.astro";
---

<ContentPage
	title="Features | PAN Card Photo & Signature Resizer"
	description="Explore portal-specific PAN photo and signature presets for NSDL/Protean and UTIITSL, adjustable dimensions, JPEG export, and private in-browser processing."
	canonicalUrl="https://nsdlphotoresize.com/features/"
	eyebrow="Tool features"
	heading="Useful features for PAN card photo and signature resizing"
	intro="Prepare both image types with a focused online PAN card tool. Adjust the crop and dimensions, review a JPEG preview, and keep image processing on your device."
>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Photo and signature modes</h2>
		<p>
			Switch between Photograph and Signature modes, then choose
			NSDL/Protean or UTIITSL to load that portal’s reference dimensions,
			resolution, and file-size limit. NSDL/Protean uses a 2.5 × 3.5 cm
			photo and 4.5 × 2 cm signature, both at 200 DPI and up to 50 KB.
			UTIITSL uses a 213 × 213 px photo at 300 DPI (up to 30 KB) and a
			400 × 200 px signature at 600 DPI (up to 60 KB). These are
			editable presets, not a substitute for checking current portal
			instructions.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Flexible crop and output</h2>
		<p>
			Move the crop frame to position your image and adjust its corners
			while preserving its proportions. Set the width and height in
			centimetres, choose a portal preset, and preview the resulting
			pixel dimensions. Export a JPEG within the selected portal preset’s
			file-size limit. When an image cannot meet that limit at minimum
			quality, the tool reports the issue instead of saving an oversized
			file.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section class="space-y-3">
		<h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">Local, private editing</h2>
		<p>
			Image selection, cropping, preview, and export run in your browser.
			Your image is not uploaded to this website, and the original source
			is not overwritten. Use a clear source image for the best result;
			resizing cannot restore detail lost to blur or poor lighting.
		</p>
	</section>
	<p>
		For an NSDL PAN card photo resizer or UTI PAN card photo resizer
		workflow, choose the matching preset and check the current portal
		requirements before using your downloaded file.
		<a class="text-link" href="/#requirements">Review the image requirements</a>.
	</p>
</ContentPage>
